        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "[codex] Add on-demand fusion model routing",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add `clawrouter/fusion`, an explicitly selected virtual chat model\n- run up to four bounded advisers concurrently, then synthesize with one configured final model\n- route every subcall through existing policy, budget, content-retention, readiness, and usage paths\n- add an experimental `local-openai` provider for Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, and other OpenAI-compatible servers\n- add a redesigned Access → Fusion workspace, discovery/catalog integration, docs, and diagnostics\n\n## Design and hardening\n\nFusion is one sparse adviser layer plus one final synthesizer. Adviser failures fail open. Adviser requests are text-only, exclude tool schemas and images, use bounded context/output, and are inserted into the final request as delimited untrusted evidence. The final request preserves the caller's original tools, multimodal content, streaming mode, and output contract.\n\nThe default cost-oriented profile pairs `local/qwen3:8b` with `openai/gpt-4.1-mini`. Selected models must expose OpenAI chat-completions request and response formats; incompatible provider-native chat routes are rejected. A hosted Cloudflare Worker cannot reach laptop loopback, so production local-model use requires a secured network-reachable endpoint or a locally run ClawRouter.\n\nPre-merge hardening now also:\n\n- preflights and reserves the synthesizer's worst-case configured proposal budget before advisers can spend\n- aborts timed-out adviser fetches and accounting streams, bounds response bytes before JSON parsing, and continues through the synthesizer\n- rejects malformed chat messages with a stable 400 before any upstream call\n- omits unsupported temperature fields for current OpenAI reasoning models\n- keeps dynamic `local/*` models zero-priced while leaving unknown hosted dynamic models unpriced\n- advertises Fusion only when enabled and its synthesizer route is executable for the caller\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm check` — 35 Worker, 23 admin, and 43 script tests passed; Worker/admin TypeScript passed\n- `pnpm build` — deterministic 21-provider snapshot, production Vite build, and Worker checks passed\n- `pnpm worker:e2e` — adviser → synthesizer order, budget preflight, malformed input, incompatible wire formats, timeout abort/connection close, headers, discovery, and zero-price local accounting passed\n- real Ollama `qwen3:0.6b` end-to-end through local ClawRouter — 1 adviser, 0 failures, non-empty final response\n- browser QA — desktop, tablet, and mobile; light/dark themes; no viewport overflow; selected mobile Fusion tab scrolls into view\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- each adviser and synthesizer is independently metered and retained under the caller's normal policy\n- the local provider records zero upstream API price; hardware and hosting cost remain external\n- `clawrouter/fusion` is disabled by default and advertised only when enabled and executable\n",
